  "description": "\u201cThe symmedian point of the excentral triangle, where lines joining the three excenters to the side midpoints concur.\u201d\n\u2014 Clark Kimberling's Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers (ETC) \u2022 X_9 (Mittenpunkt)\n\nInteractive GEOMETOR Explorer page: https://geometor.github.io/etc/centers/c-00001-00019/x-00009/\n\n1 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: X_9 = Mittenpunkt \u2022 [J_a M_a] \u2229 [J_b M_b] \u2229 [J_c M_c]\n2 \u00b7 GOAL: X_9 = Mittenpunkt \u2022 [J_a M_a] \u2229 [J_b M_b] \u2229 [J_c M_c]\n3 \u00b7 ASSERT: Trilinears (s-a) : (s-b) : (s-c) \u2022 Barycentrics a(s-a) : b(s-b) : c(s-c)\n4 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Line {1, 6, 9} \u2022 Line {2, 7, 9} \u2022 Line {4, 9, 10}\n5 \u00b7 INTERSECT: Line {1, 6, 9} \u2022 Line {2, 7, 9} \u2022 Line {4, 9, 10}\n6 \u00b7 PROVE: Complement of X_7 (Gergonne) \u2022 Isogonal X_57 \u2022 Isotomic X_85\n7 \u00b7 \u2234: Kimberling (6, 9, 13) Search = 3.571972699230\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 ETC \u2022 X_9",
